.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-disputes - List every dispute on your payments (requires login)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 disputes [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the disputes across the payments your wallet is party to, as payer or
payee, each with its parent payment embedded.

.PP
Open AND closed: a closed dispute stops setting the 'disputed' flag on
\&'payments list' (which reports current state) but is still listed here, so the
history stays visible. Filter with --status to see only one of the two.

.PP
Distinct from 'rail0 payments disputes \&', which is the open/close history
of ONE payment.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for disputes

.PP
\fB--page\fP=0
	Page number (1-based)

.PP
\fB--per-page\fP=0
	Results per page

.PP
\fB--sort\fP=""
	Sort fields (e.g. -opened_at)

.PP
\fB--status\fP=""
	Filter by dispute status: open or closed


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 disputes
  rail0 disputes --status open
  rail0 disputes --sort -opened_at --per-page 50
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0(1)\fP, \fBrail0-disputes-reasons(1)\fP
